  "final_text": "Both objects exist and are saved as specified. The rule is enabled, and its last run reported status `ok`.\n\n**Data exploration** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, about 14,074 documents)\n- Key fields: `@timestamp` (time field), `response` (HTTP status, with `response.keyword` for aggregation), `request`/`url`, `clientip`/`geo.dest`, `bytes`, `extension`, and `agent`.\n- Status codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). There are no other 5xx codes in this data.\n- Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, so part of the data is in the future relative to today (2026-10-11).\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-ee10d453 Web logs overview\"** (id `592e3f0c-871e-42ff-b86a-ce4ebe0b9d1a`)\n- Total requests (metric)\n- 5xx responses (metric)\n- Requests over time (line)\n- Responses by status code (bar, top 10)\n- All panels use ES|QL against `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n\n**Rule: \"EFF-ee10d453 5xx spike\"** (id `5e6fbb73-91ad-4947-a7d7-fdef461d5d40`)\n- Type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, enabled.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` over the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- No actions are attached, so it only records alerts in Kibana.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- The dashboard time range is absolute, 2026-10-01 to 2026-12-31, so the panels show the sample data. Change it if you want a relative range.\n- I used the Dashboards API for the dashboard and the alerting API for the rule.\n- Kibana's console and ES|QL endpoints aren't exposed here, so I ran the exploration queries through the internal search endpoint.\n\n**Not verified:** I didn't confirm the rule has fired. With 5xx responses only at 503 and timestamps mostly outside the trailing 5-minute window, it may stay quiet until data arrives in that window.",
